1
00:00:00,357 --> 00:00:02,503
McDonald's million-dollar Monopoly winners

2
00:00:02,513 --> 00:00:04,793
were picked in an airport bathroom stall.

3
00:00:04,948 --> 00:00:06,991
By the man hired to protect them.

4
00:00:07,189 --> 00:00:08,382
Jerry Jacobson.

5
00:00:08,441 --> 00:00:09,356
Ex-cop.

6
00:00:09,415 --> 00:00:10,970
Head of security for the company running

7
00:00:10,980 --> 00:00:11,626
the game.

8
00:00:11,780 --> 00:00:12,500
His job?

9
00:00:12,559 --> 00:00:14,706
Escort the winning pieces, with an auditor

10
00:00:14,716 --> 00:00:16,248
watching his every move.

11
00:00:16,446 --> 00:00:18,801
Then a supplier slipped up, and mailed

12
00:00:18,811 --> 00:00:20,910
Jerry a box of tamper-proof seals.

13
00:00:21,022 --> 00:00:23,214
Now he could reseal the envelopes, and

14
00:00:23,224 --> 00:00:24,215
nobody would know.

15
00:00:24,370 --> 00:00:26,467
So he'd slip into airport stalls...

16
00:00:26,526 --> 00:00:28,546
and swap the winners for duds.

17
00:00:28,657 --> 00:00:29,920
Then he sold them.

18
00:00:29,978 --> 00:00:30,963
To family.

19
00:00:31,022 --> 00:00:31,972
To friends.

20
00:00:31,996 --> 00:00:33,850
To strangers paying cash.

21
00:00:34,048 --> 00:00:36,577
For years, almost every top prize went

22
00:00:36,587 --> 00:00:37,641
to his network.

23
00:00:37,717 --> 00:00:39,607
Over twenty million dollars.

24
00:00:39,805 --> 00:00:42,425
Then an anonymous tip reached the FBI.

25
00:00:42,501 --> 00:00:44,114
Jerry got thirty-seven months.

26
00:00:44,347 --> 00:00:46,493
Prosecutors say even the million-dollar

27
00:00:46,503 --> 00:00:48,285
piece mailed to a children's hospital

28
00:00:48,295 --> 00:00:49,340
came from Jerry.

29
00:00:49,668 --> 00:00:51,487
So next time you peel one...

30
00:00:51,563 --> 00:00:53,277
ask who touched it first.

